.bazelbsp
tmp
# Sub-modules: these directories have their own MODULE.bazel and are
# developed/tested independently (cd <dir> && bazelisk test ...).
# Excluding them from //... keeps the root module fast by avoiding
# heavy deps (kepler-formal).

lec
naja
test/docker
bazel-orfs-bazel-dev

# Claude Code keeps its worktrees under .claude/worktrees, each with its
# own bazel-<name> convenience symlink into an output base. Root-level
# bazel-* symlinks are ignored by bazel itself; nested ones are not, so
# //... would walk into another checkout's external repos and fail on
# the first repo the root module does not know.
.claude
